--- Two corrections to the citations above ---
The grep for the README's statement missed the first one because it wraps across lines:
    README.md: The website is the one part of this that is reachable from off the Mac: it listens on every
    README.md: network interface, and the API behind it has no password. Anyone who can reach port 7788 on the
    README.md: same network — a shared or untrusted Wi-Fi, say — can read every kept conversation, start,
    README.md: pause and steer runs, change the topic and the seats, upload documents, and open any share
And the `bind 127.0.0.1` line that matters is the insertion, not the comment:
    tools/start.sh:       # the generated copy gets one and the listener becomes 127.0.0.1:$PORT.
    tools/start.sh:       sed -e "/^http:\/\/:$PORT {/a\\
    tools/start.sh: 	bind 127.0.0.1" "$CONFIG" > "$CONFIG.local-only"
    tools/start.sh:       mv "$CONFIG.local-only" "$CONFIG"
    tools/start.sh:       dim "binding the website to 127.0.0.1 only (--local-only)"

